    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d683">

                <pb facs="0799" n="739" xml:id="pg739"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Gresham</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge, with
                    thanks, your notes, Nos. 20 and 22, of the 26th and 30th instant, respectively,
                    forwarding information relative to fire on cotton ships in certain parts of the
                    United States.</p>
                <p>I have not failed to communicate the contents of these notes to Her Majesty’s
                    Government, arid I shall be very grateful for any further information which may
                    reach you respecting the origin of the fires on board the cotton ships at New
                    Orleans.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian Pauncefote</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
